// Conformance: file imports (SPEC.md section 15).
//
// `import "imports-lib.ufy";` resolves relative to THIS file's own
// directory (test/conformance/), so it finds the sibling file right next
// to it regardless of the process's current working directory.
//
// Expected stdout, in order:
//   print: circle
//   print: square
//   print: circle
//   print: square
//   print: red
//
// - The first "circle"/"square" pair comes from imports-lib.ufy's OWN
//   query, running at the point of the import below -- BEFORE anything
//   that follows in this file, proving imports are processed inline/
//   interleaved, not deferred to the end.
// - The second "circle"/"square" pair is this file's own query, reusing
//   is_shape/1 (defined only in imports-lib.ufy) -- proving the imported
//   clauses are visible here.
// - The duplicate `import` below is a silent no-op (once-semantics, like
//   #pragma once): imports-lib.ufy's facts/rule/query are NOT registered
//   or run a second time, so there is no second "circle"/"square" pair
//   from it.
// - The final "red" comes from color/1, defined only in this file, proving
//   the importer's own definitions after the import still work normally.

import "imports-lib.ufy";

query {
    is_shape( $x );
    print( $x );
}

import "imports-lib.ufy";

color( red );

query {
    color( $x );
    print( $x );
}
